---
source: crates/odx-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: cmd.render_long_help().to_string()
---
Run the gitaggregate-compatible drop-in (same as `git-aggregate-rs`)

Usage: odx git-aggregate [OPTIONS] [ACTION]

Arguments:
  [ACTION]
          Action to run

          Possible values:
          - aggregate:       Fetch and merge the configured branches and pull requests
          - show-closed-prs: List pull requests in the configuration that are closed or merged
          - show-all-prs:    List every pull request in the configuration with its state
          
          [default: aggregate]

Options:
  -c, --config <FILE>
          Path to the repositories file
          
          [default: repos.yaml]

  -p, --push
          Push the result to the target remote and branch

  -d, --dirmatch <PATTERN>
          Only process target directories matching this fnmatch pattern

      --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>
          Logging verbosity

          Possible values:
          - debug:    Everything
          - info:     Progress per repository
          - warning:  Warnings and errors
          - error:    Errors only
          - critical: Errors only (git-aggregator's highest level)
          
          [default: info]

  -e, --expand-env
          Expand `$VAR` and `${VAR}` in the repositories file

      --env-file <FILE>
          Variables for --expand-env (the environment takes precedence)

  -f, --force
          Discard local changes, and replace directories not built by odx

  -j, --jobs <N>
          Repositories fetched and built at once [default: number of CPUs]

      --no-color
          Disable colored output

      --allow-shell
          Run `shell_command_after` entries (skipped with a warning otherwise)

      --rebase
          Rebase merges onto the result instead of creating merge commits

      --mergiraf
          Resolve conflicts with mergiraf (`ODX_MERGIRAF` names the executable)

      --json
          Machine-readable summary on stdout

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
  -C, --project-dir <DIR>
          Run as if started in DIR

      --offline
          Serve forge and index data from the cache only; a repository not in the cache yet is still fetched. Local work (git, pre-commit, odoo-lint) takes as long as before

      --fresh
          Ignore cached data; refresh everything before answering

      --no-refresh
          Use cached data even when stale. Like --offline, this saves network time only

      --refresh-index
          Rebuild the addon index for the series involved

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase log verbosity (repeatable)

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only
